{"raw": {"https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Adjunct-Nursing Faculty.html": {"title": "Adjunct Nursing Faculty", "description": "Adjunct Nursing Faculty | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Adjunct-Nursing Faculty Adjunct Nursing Faculty Date Posted: December 15, 2025 Job Title: Adjunct-Nursing Faculty General Summary : Faculty teach an average of 12 hours of load per academic year. Academic load can be made up of face-to-face courses, hybrid courses, and/or clinical/lab/simulation experiences. Teaching assignments will be made in collaboration with the Nursing Program Director and the Dean of the School of Health Professions. Primary Duties & Responsibilities : Plan and deliver learning experiences for nursing students to make maximum use of class/lab/clinical time. Complete assigned nursing education load. Deliver assigned didactic (classroom) lectures using effective, evidence-based teaching strategies by facilitating student learning through interactive activities, case studies, discussion, and other activities as appropriate for the course. Evaluate student performance. Evaluation of student performance in classroom includes evaluation of papers, projects, and journals, etc. and returning these to students in timely fashion. Attend department meetings and participate in committees as assigned. Hold office hours or provide scheduled availability for student questions, or clarification of course content. Identify students requiring academic intervention and refer to appropriate support services Uphold all institutional, state board of nursing, and accreditation requirements, including the Missouri State Board of Nursing Minimum Standards Perform other duties as assigned. Education & Experience Qualifications For undergraduate pre-licensure programs: MSN preferred Teaching experience preferred RN, MSN-in-Process within one year of graduation mandatory. Current, unencumbered, Missouri nursing license. Approval by the Missouri State Board of Nursing as a faculty member. Physical Requirements For face-to-face courses: Frequently stand for at least one hour consecutively. Operate classroom audio-visual equipment. Speak loudly and clearly enough to be understood by students. Other Skills & Abilities: Communication: The faculty member must be able to utilize effective communication with peers, students, clients and their families, and other healthcare providers. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to read at a competency level that allows one to safely carry out the essential functions of an assignment (examples: handwritten documentation, printed policy and procedure manuals, clinical guidelines and instructions, course syllabi). Ability to effectively interpret and process information. Ability to effectively communicate (verbally and in writing) with students, peers, clients/families, healthcare professionals, and others within the community. Ability to access information and to communicate and document effectively via computer. Ability to recognize, interpret, and respond to nonverbal behavior of self and others. Behavior: The faculty member must be capable of exercising good judgment, developing empathetic and therapeutic relationships with students, clients and others, and tolerating close and direct physical contact with a diverse population. They will include people of all ages, races, socioeconomic and ethnic backgrounds, as well as individuals with weight disorders, physicals disfigurement, and medical and mental health problems. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to work with multiple clients/families and colleagues at the same time. Ability to foster and maintain cooperative and collegial relationships with students and peers. Critical Thinking: The faculty member must possess sufficient abilities in the areas of calculation, critical problem solving, reasoning, and judgment to be able to comprehend and process information within a reasonable time frame as determined by the profession. The faculty member must be able to prioritize, organize, and attend to talks and responsibilities efficiently. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to collect, interpret and analyze written, verbal and observed data about students. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks, integrate information and make decisions. Ability to apply knowledge of the principles, indications, and contraindications for nursing interventions. Ability to act safely and ethically in the classroom, simulation/skills lab, and in the community. Other Information & Attributes: This position requires a minimum of 12 hours of academic load per year. Overload can be negotiated. Serves as an effective, collegial member of nursing faculty. Contributes to monitoring and evaluating of students. Supports the work and efforts of colleagues in achieving the programmatic, departmental, and institutional mission and vision. Engages collaboratively in the development and attainment of program and course goals. Seeks innovative, cost-effective solutions to programmatic, departmental, and institutional challenges. Exercises effective time management by developing and maintaining timelines for personal tasks and student learning activities. Prioritizes instructional responsibilities and guides students in managing their academic workload Demonstrates an understanding of substantial higher education issues. Participates actively in appropriate state, regional and national professional organizations, as well as community groups. CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.\u00a0 They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.\u00a0\u00a0 Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9 2026"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Dean of School of Health Professionals.html": {"title": "Dean of School of Health Professionals", "description": "Dean of School of Health Professionals | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Dean of School of Health Professionals Dean of School of Health Professionals Date Posted: September 21, 2026 Job Title: Dean of the School of Health Professions GENERAL SUMMARY : This is a 12-month administrative position with faculty rank. Responsible for the development, accreditation, and oversight of Health Professions programming in the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) and the College of Graduate and Extended Studies (CGES). PRINCIPLE DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : 30% Monitor the function of the School of Health Professions programs and faculty to maintain program effectiveness, accreditation standard compliance, and budgetary parameters; 30% Act in conjunction with the Program Director for each program of study to assure the cohesion, caliber, and accreditation of the education programs. 15% Market programs to the healthcare community, inclusive of prospective students and faculty. 25% Work closely with the Associate Provost for Innovation to enhance all aspects of the provision of education, the financial accountability of programming, the well-being of all faculty, staff, and students, and the general good reputation enjoyed by CMU. Perform other duties as assigned. MANAGERIAL/SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES : At least 75-100% of time is spent in managerial capacity. Directly supervises Program Directors, the Clinical Coordinators, and staff. Overload may be negotiated. Evaluate Program Directors, faculty, and staff performance annually and as needed. Discuss evaluations with faculty and provide copy to the Provost\u2019s office, and the employee file. Guide faculty development. Resource day-to-day programmatic management by the Program Directors. Oversee the resolution of programmatic issues and complaints. Attend programmatic, departmental, and institutional faculty meetings. Participate in the recruitment and retention of students; Approve contractual agreements with clinical agencies prior to their submission to Senior Staff for signature. Liaison with the Assistant Dean of Online Programming to assure course structure and schedule parameters are communicated to Program Directors and remain in congruence with CMU guidelines and requirements; Ensure the Program Coordinators for the BSN-G, BSN-C, and ABSN maintain the congruency of coursework and evaluation strategies for the bachelor\u2019s-level programs; Ensure appropriate faculty recruitment; Provide leadership to the faculty in curriculum development, implementation and evaluation; Serve on University-wide, CLAS, or CGES committees as requested; Oversee the accreditation processes for all programs and ensure appropriate compliance with standards; Meet regularly with Program Directors. Preside at Divisional meetings. Oversee the development of programmatic budgets and submit them to the Provost of the University. Oversee budget expenditures. Provide leadership in total program assessment/revision and new program development. Assist with development and implementation of new graduate programs. Further professional development by participation in professional organizations and/or continuing education programs and workshops. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Administrative experience preferred. PhD in nursing or related field (with MSN) or DNP required Current, unencumbered, Missouri nursing license. Approval by the Missouri State Board of Nursing as a faculty member. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Frequently stand and/or sit for at least one hour consecutively. Operate classroom and meeting audio-visual equipment. Speak loudly and clearly enough to be understood by students. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Communication: The Program Administrator must be able to utilize effective communication with peers, subordinates, students and their families, other educational providers, and other constituents of the community of interest. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to effectively interpret and process written and verbal information. Ability to effectively communicate (verbally and in writing). Ability to access information and to communicate and document effectively via computer. Ability to recognize, interpret, and respond to nonverbal behavior of self and others. Consistently demonstrate a professional presentation that upholds the Central Methodist University mission statements and philosophy. Behavior: The Program Administrator must be capable of exercising good judgment, developing empathetic and therapeutic relationships with others. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to work with multiple students/families and colleagues at the same time. Ability to foster and maintain cooperative and collegial relationships with students, faculty, and peers. Ability to provide faculty leadership and support faculty development. Critical Thinking: The Program Administrator must possess sufficient abilities in the areas of calculation, critical problem solving, reasoning, and judgment to be able to comprehend and process information within a reasonable time frame. The Program Administrator must be able to prioritize, organize, and attend to responsibilities efficiently. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to collect, interpret and analyze written, verbal and observed data. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks, integrate information and make decisions. Ability to apply knowledge of the principles, indications, and contraindications for nursing educational processes. Ability to act safely and ethically in the classroom and in the community. Ability to lead others in a professional manner. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: Serves as an effective, collegial member of the faculty. Supports the work and efforts of colleagues in achieving the programmatic, departmental, and institutional mission and vision. Contributes creatively and helpfully to setting and meeting goals. Seeks innovative, cost-effective solutions to programmatic, departmental, and institutional challenges. Sets and meets timelines; prioritizes own work and that of faculty. Demonstrates an understanding of substantial higher education issues. Participates actively in appropriate state, regional and national professional organizations, as well as community groups. CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9 2026"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Faculty-Prison Education Program.html": {"title": "Faculty-Prison Education Program", "description": "Faculty-Prison Education Program | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Faculty-Prison Education Program Faculty-Prison Education Program Job Posting Date: September 30, 2026 Job Title: Faculty (Prison Education Program) Full-Time GENERAL SUMMARY : Faculty to teach individuals in Missouri correctional facilities located in Farmington and Bonne Terre, Missouri.\u00a0 Individual will be responsible for teaching Introduction to Windows, Microsoft Word, Excel and PowerPoint in a face-to-face and hybrid format. \u00a0Additional teaching responsibilities may include teaching courses such as BU225, Computer Apps in Business, face-to-face or through Lantern, and other possible courses as needed. \u00a0Teaching assignments will be made in collaboration with the Office of the Provost. This is a full-time, benefit eligible position. This position is a project-oriented instructional position with a goal of outcomes-based objectives and certification in all Microsoft products covered \u2013 Microsoft Office User Specialists (MOS). In depth coverage of Word, Excel, and PowerPoint will be covered along with document integration between the various software components and the MOS certification objectives.\u00a0 An additional focus is how these products may be used in the business setting.\u00a0 It may include additional teaching responsibilities focused on technology, software and business operations. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Plan and deliver learning experiences for students to make maximum use of class and lab time. Complete assigned teaching load both using Canvas (Lantern) and from inside the correctional facility. Deliver classroom lectures inside the correctional facility using effective, evidence-based teaching strategies by facilitating student learning through interactive activities, assignments, projects, discussion, and other activities as appropriate for the course. Evaluate student performance. Evaluation of student performance in classroom includes evaluation of assignments and projects, and returning these to students in timely fashion. Identify students requiring academic intervention and refer to appropriate support services Manage all classroom safety and security requirements Manage the testing of students for Certification on Certiport Meet all faculty requirements as outlined in the Faculty Handbook Meet all requirements as outlined by the Missouri Department of Corrections Perform other duties as assigned. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Bachelor\u2019s degree required; Master\u2019s degree preferred Microsoft User Certifications preferred Microsoft User Specialist Certification preferred Teaching experience preferred Experience with Certiport Exam delivery, proctoring, and the certification process preferred. CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9 2026"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Instructor Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano.html": {"title": "Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano", "description": "Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano Date Posted: September 18, 2026 Job Title: Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano GENERAL SUMMARY : The Swinney Conservatory of Music at Central Methodist University invites applications for a full-time non-tenure track Instructor/Assistant Professor of Collaborative Piano to begin Fall 2027 (title will be determined by achieved degree of selected candidate). The successful candidate will be an excellent pianist and musician who enjoys collaborating with students and faculty. PRINCIPLE DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : 75%: Play piano on campus for studio lessons, recital rehearsals and performances, choral rehearsals and performances, and opera productions 10%: Travel with students and faculty to regional festivals/competitions for performances and with the Chorale on their annual Fall Choir Tour 15%: Teach keyboard techniques courses, applied piano lessons, and accompanying skills as necessary; organize weekly student recital programs Be adept at playing various genres and styles of music Excellent sight-reading skills Efficient rehearsal technique Perform other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : A master\u2019s or terminal degree in music is preferred, but a bachelor\u2019s prepared candidate with sufficient skill and experience will be considered. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: The collaborative pianist must be able to rehearse for extended periods of time.\u00a0 Negotiating stairs and walking quickly between studios may be required. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Strong time management skills Strong communication skills Enthusiasm for working with college students at a variety of skill levels OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: This position will require some work in evenings, on weekends, and/or travel. CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive, and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Nursing Program Faculty.html": {"title": "Nursing Program Faculty", "description": "Nursing Program Faculty | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Nursing Program Faculty Nursing Program Faculty Job Posted: March 6, 2026 Job Title: Nursing Program Faculty General Summary : Assistant Professor teaching an average of 24 load hours per academic year. Nursing Program Faculty who has clinical load responsibilities are accountable to the Nursing Clinical Adjunct Faculty job description in addition to this one.\u00a0 The position is a 9-month contract that runs from August to May. Primary Duties & Responsibilities : Plan and deliver learning experiences for nursing students to make maximum use of class time. Teach assigned nursing education load. Evaluate student performances in the classroom. Discuss evaluations with students and return evaluation to student file. (Evaluation of student performance includes evaluation of papers, projects, and journals, and returning these to students in timely fashion.) Attend departmental (voting) and institutional faculty (non-voting) meetings. Serve on departmental committees as assigned. Participate in in clinical nursing education, if part of assigned load, abiding by the Nursing Clinical Faculty job description. Participate in the design and development of new health professions programs and in the revision of current health professions programs based on assessment data. Perform other duties as assigned. Education & Experience Qualifications : MSN preferred RN, MSN-in-Process within one year of graduation mandatory. Current, unencumbered, Missouri nursing license. Approval by the Missouri State Board of Nursing as a faculty member. Physical Requirements: Frequently stand for at least one hour consecutively. Operate classroom audio-visual equipment. Speak loudly and clearly enough to be understood by students. Other Skills & Abilities: Communication: The faculty member must be able to utilize effective communication with peers, students, clients and their families, and other healthcare providers. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to read at a competency level that allows one to safely carry out the essential functions of an assignment (examples: handwritten documentation, printed policy and procedure manuals, clinical guidelines and instructions, course syllabi). Ability to effectively interpret and process information. Ability to effectively communicate (verbally and in writing) with students, peers, clients/families, healthcare professionals, and others within the community. Ability to access information and to communicate and document effectively via computer. Ability to recognize, interpret, and respond to nonverbal behavior of self and others. Behavior: The faculty member must be capable of exercising good judgment, developing empathetic and therapeutic relationships with students, clients and others, and tolerating close and direct physical contact with a diverse population. They will include people of all ages, races, socioeconomic and ethnic backgrounds, as well as individuals with weight disorders, physicals disfigurement, and medical and mental health problems. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to work with multiple clients/families and colleagues at the same time. Ability to foster and maintain cooperative and collegial relationships with students and peers. Critical Thinking: The faculty member must possess sufficient abilities in the areas of calculation, critical problem solving, reasoning, and judgment to be able to comprehend and process information within a reasonable time frame as determined by the profession. The faculty member must be able to prioritize, organize, and attend to talks and responsibilities efficiently. This includes, but is not limited to: Ability to collect, interpret and analyze written, verbal and observed data about students. Ability to prioritize multiple tasks, integrate information and make decisions. Ability to apply knowledge of the principles, indications, and contraindications for nursing interventions. Ability to act safely and ethically in the classroom, simulation/skills lab, and in the community. Other Information and Attributes: This is a 09-month position and has a required minimum of 24 hours of academic load per year. Overload can be negotiated. Serves as an effective, collegial member of nursing faculty. Contributes to monitoring and evaluating of students. Supports the work and efforts of colleagues in achieving the programmatic, departmental, and institutional mission and vision. Contributes creatively and helpfully to setting and meeting goals. Seeks innovative, cost-effective solutions to programmatic, departmental, and institutional challenges. Sets and meets timelines; prioritizes own work and that of students. Demonstrates an understanding of substantial higher education issues. Participates actively in appropriate state, regional and national professional organizations, as well as community groups. Application Process: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.\u00a0 They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.\u00a0\u00a0 Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9 2026"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Academic Support Specialist CGES.html": {"title": "Academic Support Specialist-CGES", "description": "Academic Support Specialist-College of Graduate & Extended Studies | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Academic Support Specialist CGES Academic Support Specialist-College of Graduate & Extended Studies Posting Date: September 30, 2026 Job title: Academic Support Specialist-CGES GENERAL SUMMARY : To provide academic support to CMU\u2019s off-site locations, CGES (College of Graduate & Extended Studies).\u00a0 This includes but not limited to registration, transfer work and withdraws and day to day functions of the Registrar\u2019s Office pertaining to CGES students. This is a full-time, benefit eligible position. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Processes all CGES transfer work-50% First review/check of all CGES degree plans-30% Assist and Process registration forms/request for CGES students-10% Manages CGES wait lists-5% Process electronic updated information through CARS System-5% Maintains CGES files, filing included-5% Other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Associates degree preferred, not required. High school diploma, required. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to work at a computer for long periods of time, filing and periodic lifting up to 15lbs.\u00a0 Must be able to stand and speak to students at a counter. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: General office equipment, Microsoft Office products, Jenzabar and multi-tasking and customer service skills. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: Limited travel. CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.\u00a0 They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.\u00a0\u00a0 Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented. Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Academic Support Specialist CLAS.html": {"title": "Academic Support Specialist (CLAS)", "description": "Academic Support Specialist (CLAS) | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Academic Support Specialist (CLAS) Academic Support Specialist (CLAS) Date Posted: August 13, 2026 Job Title: Academic Support Specialist (CLAS) GENERAL SUMMARY : To provide academic support to CMU\u2019s Fayette Campus Students.\u00a0 This includes but not limited to registration, transfer work and withdraws and day to day functions of the Registrar\u2019s Office pertaining to CLAS (College of Liberal Arts & Sciences) students. This is a full-time position with benefits. This position is located on the Fayette Campus. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Process all CMU transcript requests-35% Assist with and enter the transfer work of CLAS students-20% Assist and Process all CLAS add/drop/withdraws forms-30% Manages CLAS wait lists-5% Process electronic updated information through CARS (Campus Administration & Registration System)-5% Maintains CLAS files, filing included-5% Other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Associates degree preferred, not required. High School Diploma, Required. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to work at a computer for long periods of time, filing and periodic lifting up to 15 lbs.\u00a0 Must be able to stand and speak to students at a counter. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented. Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Assistant Strength and Conditioning.html": {"title": "Assistant-Strength & Conditioning", "description": "Assistant-Strength and Conditioning | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Assistant-Strength and Conditioning Assistant-Strength and Conditioning Date Posted: October 7, 2026 Job Title: Assistant-Strength & Conditioning GENERAL SUMMARY The Assistant Strength and Conditioning position is a full-time exempt staff position (10 month, Aug-May) which helps oversee the general operation and maintenance of the Athletics' weight room, along with enforcing safety procedures.\u00a0 The Assistant for Strength and Conditioning will help coordinate all strength and conditioning activities for the Department of Athletics which includes all in-season and out-of-season programs used by CMU student-athletes. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Effectively design and safely implement strength and conditioning programs for multiple sports with differing physiological needs/concerns. Provide instruction for proper weightlifting and conditioning techniques. Ensure a safe and productive working environment, enforcing all codes of conduct. Communicate with the athletic training staff as to injury concerns and rehabilitation modifications for student-athletes. Effectively communicate with coaching staff any concerns regarding their team and/or individual student-athletes. Create and maintain a scientifically-backed training philosophy. Demonstrate and coach a variety of agility, speed, flexibility, and conditioning exercises, drills, and techniques with student-athletes across several sports programs. Monitor the daily training progress of all student-athletes; counsel student-athletes in the area of performance enhancement. Help supervise graduate students, work-study, and student interns. Performs other duties as assigned. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: 90% Strength and Conditioning Activities; 10% Other MANAGERIAL/SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: Helps supervises a graduate assistant(s) in both office and game-day settings. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Bachelor\u2019s degree; master\u2019s preferred. Experience working in intercollegiate athletics environment and strength and conditioning preferred. Must possess Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS) through the National Strength and Conditioning Association (NSCA) or Strength and Conditioning Coach Certified (SCCC) through the Collegiate Strength and Conditioning Coaches Association (CSCCa). Current standard first aid, cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR), and automated external defibrillation (AED) certifications. A strong working knowledge of basic strength training techniques. Strong motivational abilities. Evidence of ability to interact positively with student-athletes, colleagues, and the public. Evidence of strong organizational skills and effective oral and written communication skills. Take initiative and plan, organize, coordinate, and perform work in various situations where numerous and diverse demands are involved. Experience in program design with the ability to work with multiple sports. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Ability to lift 50 lbs., stand walk, and sit for extensive periods. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Proficient in Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, and Excel. Must be able to gain and maintain CMU driving approval. Weekends and evening work is required. Knowledge of NAIA and Heart of America Athletic Conference policies as they relate to the conduct of athletics, faculty, staff, and students. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.\u00a0 They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.\u00a0\u00a0 Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Coordinator Academic Advisor Clinton.html": {"title": "Coordinator/Academic Advisor-Clinton, MO", "description": "Coordinator/Academic Advisor-Clinton, MO | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Coordinator/Academic Advisor-Clinton, MO Coordinator/Academic Advisor-Clinton, MO Job Posting Date: October 2, 2026 Job Title: Coordinator/Academic Advisor-Clinton, MO (Full-time) GENERAL SUMMARY : This position serves as an education coordinator/faculty advisor for undergraduate degree programs in Child Development, Educational Studies and Certification Only and in Education in the areas of Early Childhood, Elementary, Middle School, Secondary, and Special Education; in addition, general recruitment and advising for assigned undergraduate programs. This position will be responsible for comprehensive recruitment, managing student records, building partnerships with the Assistant Dean, Dean, CGES Admissions, administrative offices, community college partners, and the community. Develops and executes outreach/marketing strategies, coordinates services to support student success, and ensures program quality and local faculty support. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Academic Advising & Services (60%) Advising & Degree/Certification Tracking: Provide personalized academic advising, evaluate transfer credits, and guide students through degree plans, DESE/district teacher certification rules, and student teaching placements. Progress Monitoring & Graduation Readiness: Regularly audit student records and degree milestones, intervene with academic support or campus referrals when needed, and assist students through final degree completion and commencement. Campus & Student Service Coordination: Connect students with institutional resources (e.g., accommodations, library, tutoring) and collaborate with university and community college personnel to ensure continuous academic support and student satisfaction. Recruitment and Retention (30%) Marketing, Outreach & Community Engagement: Execute multi-channel promotional strategies; conduct outreach activities related to partner and community events, and build pathways with partner colleges, high schools, and local organizations. Inquiry Management & Market Development: Provide prompt, professional follow-up across prospective student inquiries while identifying and pursuing new student markets (traditional, transfer, and working adults). Data-Driven Retention & Strategy Assessment: Track and evaluate enrollment and retention metrics to refine outreach and advising tactics for sustainable program growth. Collegial Leadership (10%) Campus Leadership: Deliver customer-service-driven leadership across with campus activities and operations. Extended Studies & Institutional Collaboration: Actively collaborate as a member of the CGES team to support regional goals, university strategic initiatives. Perform other duties as assigned. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Bachelor\u2019s degree, master\u2019s preferred; and five years of progressively responsible experience in an area related to the responsibilities of the position; Experience working with Microsoft Office products and enrollment management products. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Regularly required to sit for long periods of time. Travel between regional locations, regional communities, and CMU campuses. Must lift, carry, and move a minimum of 20 pounds on an occasional basis. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Must have strong advising experience and interpersonal skills. Must be committed to student success, quality programs, and degree attainment. Must show a demonstrated commitment to professional excellence and integrity and to the values, vision, and goals of Central Methodist University. Must be able to communicate articulately and compellingly in writing and in speech. Ability to set and meet timelines and prioritize own work and that of staff. Must maintain accurate and confidential records of student academic and college-related information. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Director of Financial Assistance.html": {"title": "Director of Financial Assistance", "description": "Director of Financial Assistance | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Director of Financial Assistance Director of Financial Assistance Date Posted: July 17, 2026 Job Title: Director of Financial Assistance GENERAL SUMMARY : Member of the Enrollment Management leadership team responsible for the effective administration of all financial aid programs and policies for CMU students. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Direct and manage student financial aid operations and programs Maintain institutional compliance for Title IV programs Assure proper counsel and advice to students and their families about financial aid opportunities Oversee the maintenance and integrity of information on the financial aid web page Ensure CMU programs and operations are administered in compliance with federal, state and institutional guidelines Hire, train, and supervise student financial assistance staff Keep abreast of financial aid trends, technologies and best practices Work collaboratively with appropriate University personnel to review financial processes and improvements to gain efficiencies and maximize service to students Perform other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Master\u2019s degree-Preferred Bachelor\u2019s Degree-Required; Accounting degree preferred Supervisor experience - Preferred 3-5 years of financial aid or higher education administrative experience - Preferred Excellent communication and organizational skills Knowledge of Prison Education Programs - Preferred OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: General knowledge of accounting principles and methods, data processing systems and computer software. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: Typical office setting.\u00a0\u00a0 Occasional weekend or evenings for special student events. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.\u00a0 They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.\u00a0\u00a0 Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Graduate Assistant Athletic Communications .html": {"title": "Graduate Assistant-Athletic Communications", "description": "Graduate Assistant Athletic Communications  | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Graduate Assistant Athletic Communications Graduate Assistant Athletic Communications Date Posted: May 19, 2026 Job Title: Graduate Assistant-Athletic Communications General Summary: Assist in the promotion of CMU Athletics (varsity and reserve) through the daily updating of the athletics website; writing and distributing athletics press releases, including game recaps; maintaining official CMU Athletics Facebook, Twitter and Instagram accounts; and managing home (varsity/reserve) contests, including official statistics, announcements, photos, and game programs. Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Assist in updating and maintaining of the CMU athletics website (schedules/results, rosters, photo galleries, etc.); writing, distributing, and posting athletics press releases to website; designing and printing athletics publications (game programs, gameday graphics etc.); set up and production of livestream of varsity contests, maintaining and reporting official statistics; maintain and update social media platforms including Instagram, Twitter (X), and Facebook, creation and editing of video content for the athletic department, coordinating athletics photos, photography and other assigned duties. Perform other duties as assigned. Managerial/Supervisory Responsibilities: Assist in the supervision of student workers in both office and game-day settings. Education & Experience Qualifications : Bachelor\u2019s degree in journalism, communications, sports management, or related field. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to balance multiple tasks and projects to complete them efficiently and on time. Knowledge and/or background in athletics, including statistical record keeping a plus. Excellent computer skills desirable. Physical Requirements: Some lifting up to 40 lbs. necessary. Other Skills & Abilities: Proficient in Adobe InDesign, Adobe Photoshop, Adobe Premier Pro, Microsoft Word and Microsoft Excel. Experience with Presto Stats and web page design preferred. Understanding of and open-mindedness to new technologies. Other Information & Attributes: Regularly requires evening and weekend work. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.\u00a0 They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.\u00a0\u00a0 Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Graduate Assistant Athletics Creative Content.html": {"title": "Graduate Assistant-Athletics/Creative Content", "description": "Graduate Assistant-Athletics-Creative Content | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Graduate Assistant-Athletics-Creative Content Graduate Assistant-Athletics-Creative Content Date Posted: May 20, 2026 Job Title: Graduate Assistant-Athletics/Creative Content General Summary: Support the communications efforts for the athletics department and its 22 varsity sports and eight reserve sports by contributing high-quality photos and video content, coordinating social media efforts, and producing marketing content to enhance the game day experience. Primary Duties & Responsibilities: Shooting, producing, and editing video content for various platforms; Assisting with the photography and videography of media days; Brainstorm, create, and publish both graphic and video content across the athletic department\u2019s social media channels (Twitter, Facebook, Instagram), website, YouTube, and other platforms; Contribute to the maintenance, organization, and oversight of the overall content calendar; Perform other duties as assigned. Managerial/Supervisory Responsibilities: Assist in the supervision of student workers in both office and game-day settings. Education & Experience Qualifications : Bachelor\u2019s degree within the preferred area of study of Digital Media, Film, and Broadcasting, Communications, Journalism, Public Relations, or Sports Management. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Ability to balance multiple tasks and projects in order to complete them efficiently and on time. Knowledge and/or background in athletics, Excellent computer skills desirable. Physical Requirements: Some lifting up to 40 lbs. necessary. Other Skills & Abilities: Proficient or basic knowledge of Adobe Creative Suite programs (Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere Pro, After Effects); Experience in advanced content creation, including video and photo shooting and editing skills; An understanding of relevant social media platforms Other Information & Attributes: Regularly requires evening and weekend work. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.\u00a0 They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.\u00a0Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/job-listing1.html": {"title": "Graduate Assistant-Strength & Conditioning", "description": "Graduate Assistant-Strength and Conditioning | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Graduate Assistant-Strength and Conditioning Graduate Assistant-Strength and Conditioning Date Posted: December 8, 2025 Job Title: Graduate Assistant-Strength & Conditioning General Summary : Responsibilities include working with all phases of the strength and conditioning program that include but are not limited to: working with various athletic programs to develop physical strength, flexibility, speed, and agility utilizing program(s) designed to each athletic program\u2019s needs.\u00a0 Coordinating with athletic staff on scheduling and the status of the program and /or student-athletes.\u00a0 Promoting a positive atmosphere in the facility.\u00a0 Assisting with the general upkeep of equipment and the facility. Other duties as assigned. Develop a familiarity with NAIA rules and maintain the integrity of the athletic program through the appropriate application of these rules. Provide excellent customer service to our students, donors, sponsors, alumni and all of our internal and external constituents. Primary Duties & Responsibilities : 70% - Work with various athletic programs on strength and conditioning 20% - Coordinate with athletic staff 10% - Other duties as assigned Education & Experience Qualifications : Bachelor's Degree required.\u00a0 Bachelor\u2019s degree in exercise science or related field preferred. First Aid/ CPR/AED certification. Progress towards CSCS and/or SCCC certification (preference to those already certified). Previous experience in college athletics preferred. Must be accepted in to the graduate program at Central Methodist University. Physical Requirements: Ability to lift 50lbs, stand on your feet for periods of three to five hours.\u00a0 Bending, walking, kneeling, stretching, and stooping. Set up equipment and facility as needed Other Skills & Abilities: Ability to communicate effectively in both written and verbal form.\u00a0 Experience with Microsoft Word. Other Information & Attributes: . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.\u00a0 They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.\u00a0\u00a0 Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Campus Safety Officer.html": {"title": "Campus Safety Officer", "description": "Campus Safety Officer | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Campus Safety Officer Campus Safety Officer Date Posted: August 18, 2026 Job Title: Campus Safety Officer G GENERAL SUMMARY : Professional safety officer to provide excellent customer service to our students, faculty and staff.\u00a0\u00a0 Provide protection to assets, personnel, and students and to report any suspicious behavior on and around campus to authorities. \u00a0This person will maintain a highly visible presence and promote a safe, secure and responsible campus atmosphere.Detecting, deterring, observing and reporting are key duties. This is a full-time position. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Protect University employees, students and property by promoting a safe campus and safety awareness. Observe campus and facilities for signs of crime, vandalism and unsafe behavior and investigate as needed. Initiate proactive means of protecting life or property. Take accurate notes and make reports of unusual or suspicious occurrences. Regularly patrol campus and facilities. Monitor and control access at building entrances. Monitor parking lots and enforce parking regulations. Monitor alarm systems and video cameras and operate emergency systems. Perform basic First Aid, CPR and AED. Assist Grounds and Maintenance with snow removal Perform other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : High School diploma or GED. Work experience as a security/safety guard or in a related field. Customer Service Experience. Ability to operate vehicles and equipment and valid driver\u2019s license. Excellent knowledge of public safety and security procedures/protocols. Surveillance skills and attention to detail. ALICE training (Can be provided on site). PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to lift 75lbs. Must be able to spend extended periods on foot whether standing or walking in varying weather conditions. Must be able to work in extreme weather conditions. Must be able to climb stairs, and ladders. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Computer knowledge to send and receive email messages. Word processing (Daily Safety Activity Reports). Microsoft Excel (data entry) Understanding of Campus Alert System and how it works. Basic understanding of smart phone systems and usage. Integrity and professionalism OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: The standard schedule for this position is 12:00 a.m. \u2013 12:00 p.m. on Saturdays and Sundays and 4:00 p.m. \u2013 12:00 a.m. on Monday & Tuesdays. Schedule is subject to change based on operational needs, including staffing levels, call-ins, approved time off, or adjustments made by the supervisor. Work Schedules will include working on holidays and as needed for special events. Pre-employment Background Screening required. This is an essential personnel position and is required to be on campus during designated work hours. Essential security positions are required to be at work even if campus is closed due to inclement weather. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9 2026"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Housekeeping 2nd Shift.html": {"title": "Position Title: Housekeeping- 2ndShift (1:00 pm-9:30 pm)", "description": "Housekeeping- 2nd Shift | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Housekeeping 2nd Shift Housekeeping- 2nd Shift Position Title: Housekeeping- 2 nd Shift (1:00 pm-9:30 pm) GENERAL SUMMARY: Perform a regular cleaning schedule for campus facilities. Report any maintenance problems. Maintain public restrooms, shower rooms and building and hall common area.\u00a0 This position is full time position and is benefit eligible.\u00a0 The opening is for 2 nd shift, Mon \u2013 Fri 1:00pm \u2013 9:30pm - Shift hours are flexible. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Ensure the assigned departmental building areas are cleaned on a scheduled basis. Remove trash to designated pickup points. Report building system problems to Facilities office. Adequately stock restrooms with paper products and soap. Disinfect designated areas as required. Strip and recoat designated floors. Clean carpets and floor tile. Perform full housekeeping duties during assigned work hours. Other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : One year in Custodial Services preferred. High School diploma preferred. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Must be able to lift 50 lbs. Full range of physical motion. Operate a variety of cleaning equipment. Work in some heat extremes during summer. Must be able to navigate up and down stairs OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Must be able to work with other housekeeping staff as a team, as well as cover other buildings when short staffed. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: Occasional overtime and weekend work for special events. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU Employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole.\u00a0 They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of CMU.\u00a0\u00a0 Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time.html": {"title": "Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time", "description": "Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-Time Job Title: \u00a0Prison Education Program Study Hall Coordinator Part-time Date Posted:\u00a0 2/16/2026 Reports To: Provost FLSA Classification:\u00a0 Non-Exempt GENERAL SUMMARY : This is a part-time position that works within the state of Missouri Correctional Facilities to provide support for prison education program students. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Hold study hall for a set period of time, dependent on correctional facility Check high school equivalency information in AS 400 Regularly review conduct violations of students for continued participation in AS400 Manage the call out list for study hall each week Manage the Lantern class for communication for the correctional facility Assist students with questions Assist with registration and financial aid activities, as needed Perform other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred.\u00a0 Correctional facility experience is preferred. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Frequently stand and/or sit for several hours consecutively. May work in buildings without elevator access, requiring routine use of stairways to move between floors. May work in areas of a facility without air conditioning. OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Microsoft Office experience preferred, Canvas LMS experience preferred, AS400 experience preferred OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: This position may require travel, evenings, use of a personal vehicle, and required to enter a correctional facility. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. APPLY TODAY CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Systems Support Specialist PEP.html": {"title": "Prison Education Program Systems Support Specialist", "description": "Prison Education Program Systems Support Specialist | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Prison Education Program Systems Support Specialist Prison Education Program Systems Support Specialist Job Posting Date: September 30, 2026 Job Title: Prison Education Program Systems Support Specialist GENERAL SUMMARY : The purpose of this position is to support the Prison Education Program by maintaining Department of Corrections systems (e.g. MOCIS), Lantern, Jenzabar, and will assist with tracking, updating and communication related to transfers, graduations, and violation and other removals. In addition, this position will support the review of conduct violations weekly.\u00a0 May also provide support to other areas of the PEP program as requested. This is a full-time, benefit eligible position. PRIMARY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Updating MOCIS \u201345% Tracking Transfers-5% Tracking Graduations-5% Updating Lantern and Jenzabar-10% Submitting Letters to Facilities due to removal for students-20% Tracking and removal of apps from Lantern-5% Assist with tracking of violations and notifying facilities-10% Perform other duties as assigned EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Able to sit for extended periods of time OTHER SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Microsoft Office experience preferred. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: This position is maintained at the Central Office for the Missouri Department of Corrections and the individual must work from this location.\u00a0 Must pass all background checks and be eligible to work within a correctional facility and undergo all relevant trainings. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}, "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Project Coordinator Title III Grant.html": {"title": "Project Coordinator", "description": "Project Coordinator - Title III Grant | Central Methodist University Close Apply myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Library Pay Deposit Locations Give to CMU About Office of the President History Accreditation Event Calendar Student Parking Campus Attractions Visiting CMU Offices Faculty & Staff Directory Student Consumer Information Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Online Programs Catalogs Dual Credit Registrar\u2019s Office Center for Learning and Teaching Digital U Course Schedules Library Services Academic Calendar Graduation Information Request Transcript Transfer Guides Admissions & Aid Schedule a Visit Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Business Office Find Your Counselor Eagle Days Apply Now Request More Information Scholarship Opportunities Financial Assistance Veteran-Military Central Experience Student Life Student Services & Resources Residence Life Dining at CMU Campus Safety International Students Career Development Center Clubs & Organizations Schedule a Visit Eagle Bookstore Fine Arts Center for Faith and Service Alumni Make A Gift Meet Our Team Make a Difference Stay Connected Career Development Center Eagle Pride Alumni Events Alumni Association Alumni Awards Talon Athletics I Am A... Prospective Student Visiting Student Parent Alumni & Friend Visitor Current Student Faculty & Staff International Learner MENU About Academics Admissions Athletics Student Life Aid / Scholarships Locations Apply Pay Deposit Library Transcripts Alumni / Giving Canvas myCMU Eagle Mail Home All Employment Opportunities Human Resources at CMU Offices at CMU About CMU Project Coordinator-Title III Grant Project Coordinator - Title III Grant Date Posted: October 12, 2026 Job Title: Project Coordinator - Title III Grant GENERAL SUMMARY : Coordinate a five-year two-million-dollar grant received by the University from the Department of Education (DOE), working under the Vice President for Enrollment Management. This position is funded by a federal grant, located on the Fayette Campus and benefit eligible. PRINCIPLE DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Work with the VPEM to ensure all areas of the grant are moving forward in a timely manner as written in the grant application. Serve as a member of the Fiscal Year End Task Force. Work with external vendors to ensure timely delivery of goods and services. Communicate professionally and effectively to all grant stakeholders, internal and external, on a regular basis. Schedule any necessary meetings and follow-up with stakeholders on all activities related to the grant. At all times, have a clear understanding of objectives and the progress toward each objective. Work with the Principal Investigator and the Business Office to receive all payments, submit reports, etc. Work with all stakeholders to gather evidence for reports, etc. Write all reports and submit all documentation as required by the DOE or equivalent. Perform other duties as assigned. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE QUALIFICATIONS : Bachelor\u2019s degree required. Higher education experience preferred. Excellent communication and organizational skills. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Office work, sedentary environment. OTHER INFORMATION AND ATTRIBUTES: Typical office setting. Occasional weekend or evenings. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Click below to apply and contact our Human Resource's department if you have further questions or concerns HR@centralmethodist.edu or 660-248-6899. Apply Today CMU employees provide collegial, collaborative contributions to their areas and the University as a whole. They should stimulate a harmonious, productive and inviting work environment that is customer service oriented.\u00a0 Each must maintain a commitment to the mission and purposes of Central Methodist University. Central Methodist is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and responsibilities associated with it.\u00a0 CMU management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. 877-CMU-1854 411 Central Methodist Square, Fayette, Missouri 65248 Accreditation Contact Us Coronavirus Information Employment Event Calendar Campus Safety myCMU Canvas Eagle Mail Faculty & Staff Directory Terms of Use & Privacy Policy Central Methodist University Copyright \n    \t\t\t\t\u00a9"}}, "rows": {"https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Adjunct-Nursing Faculty.html": {"school_id": 708, "posting_url": "https://centralmethodist.edu/about/offices/human-resources/jobs-fayette/listings/Adjunct-Nursing Faculty.html", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Nursing Faculty", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "School of Health Professions", "area_key_words": "Nursing", "deadline_of_applica